{
  "an11.2:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 11.2 ",
  "an11.2:0.2": "1. Dependence ",
  "an11.2:0.3": "Making a Wish ",
  "an11.2:1.1": "“Mendicants, an ethical person, who has fulfilled ethical conduct, need not make a wish: ",
  "an11.2:1.2": "‘May I have no regrets!’ ",
  "an11.2:1.3": "It’s only natural that an ethical person has no regrets. ",
  "an11.2:2.1": "When you have no regrets you need not make a wish: ",
  "an11.2:2.2": "‘May I feel joy!’ ",
  "an11.2:2.3": "It’s only natural that joy springs up when you have no regrets. ",
  "an11.2:3.1": "When you feel joy you need not make a wish: ",
  "an11.2:3.2": "‘May I experience rapture!’ ",
  "an11.2:3.3": "It’s only natural that rapture arises when you’re joyful. ",
  "an11.2:4.1": "When your mind is full of rapture you need not make a wish: ",
  "an11.2:4.2": "‘May my body become tranquil!’ ",
  "an11.2:4.3": "It’s only natural that your body becomes tranquil when your mind is full of rapture. ",
  "an11.2:5.1": "When your body is tranquil you need not make a wish: ",
  "an11.2:5.2": "‘May I feel bliss!’ ",
  "an11.2:5.3": "It’s only natural to feel bliss when your body is tranquil. ",
  "an11.2:6.1": "When you feel bliss you need not make a wish: ",
  "an11.2:6.2": "‘May my mind be immersed in samādhi!’ ",
  "an11.2:6.3": "It’s only natural for the mind to become immersed in samādhi when you feel bliss. ",
  "an11.2:7.1": "When your mind is immersed in samādhi you need not make a wish: ",
  "an11.2:7.2": "‘May I